black widow introduced viewers to a ton  of russian superheroes  and super villains straight out of the  pages of marvel comics  but how do black widow and the rest of  the cast compare with their comics  incarnations  natalia alianova romanov aka natasha  romanov was created in 1964 as femme  fatale madame natasha  sent by khrushchev to seduce and  distract tony stark  after being foiled by iron man black  widow goes on the run for months  avoiding a return to russia and a  confrontation with her superiors over  her failure  in these early appearances natasha's  look is definitely more spy  and less super villain it's when the  character returned in june 1966 as a  brainwashed supervillain in avengers  issue 29 that she got her first  costume which included fishnet stockings  a cape clasped with a bee around her  neck  and a mask after a few more years black  widow decided to reinvent herself as a  superhero  by going after spider-man drawing one of  his jay jonah jameson imposed public  ministries no less  and done the black cat suit so commonly  associated with her image in the comics  as well as the mcu so far marvel hasn't  exactly been adventurous when it comes  to black widow's look in the mcu  just about the only part of her  appearance to change has been her hair  which has gone through a few different  styles and colours most notably when she  went from red-headed to blonde  after the events of captain america  civil war which puts her at odds with  the united states government and made  her  a fugitive along with the rest of cap's  crew although she's been known to wear  office attire or even an evening gown  when she's undercover  or on assignment her battle suits  throughout the first decade of the  franchise  have pretty much all been basically  black however that changes with the  black widow movie  which gives her a brand new outfit and  pulls back the curtain on natasha's  mysterious past  prior to joining up with the avengers  one black widow's suit we haven't seen  in previous mcu films  is what's become known in the comics as  the tactical suit  first introduced to audiences in the  2010 four issue miniseries  black widow deadly origin it was  designed specifically to blend into  snowy landscapes  so the suit's utility in the russian  tundra is undeniable  and this new outfit definitely comes in  handy during natasha's 2021 solo outing  in order to find the location of the red  room black widow and her adoptive sister  elena bolova  have to fly into a russian prison and  break out their old adoptive dad  alexei shostakov and with all that snow  the tactical suit  totally fits the moment while she does  spend the majority of the movie wearing  her traditional black outfit  her time in white drawing black widow is  a nod to the characters illustrious  comics past  one of the new characters introduced in  black widow is yelena bulova  a fellow spy who's a graduate of the  infamous red room when natasha was  trained as a girl  essentially she's another black widow on  top of that she's natasha's adoptive  sister  and someone who feels a little hurt  about her big sis running off  joining the avengers and leaving her  behind bolova's first comic appearance  came in in humans volume 2  issue 5 in 1999 and in the years since  she's co-headlined several mini-series  with natasha under the black widow  mantle  in comics form elena likes to wear crop  tops and spandex  not exactly practical when fighting in  the film however pugh's elena dresses  more appropriately for combat  and she's definitely got a thing for  vests that are full of pockets  rachel vice joins the ranks of academy  award-winning actors in the mcu  by playing melina vastakov in the black  widow movie here molina is a spy  dedicated to the course of the red room  when we first meet her she's living  under cover in america  raising natasha and elena alongside  alexei shostakov  later on we find out that she's a key  player in developing the techniques that  the villainous drakov uses to control  the widows  although she eventually comes to see the  error of her waist  in the comics vostakov is known as the  iron maiden a russian assassin with deep  ties to natasha  her costume of choice is a flexible full  body armor that increases her strength  as well as protecting her from damage  unfortunately that awesome outfit  doesn't show up in the film  instead molina wears a more traditional  black widow suit  and while it lacks the intimidating  armor of iron maiden's comic book attire  it's still a pretty fantastic costume  one of the few characters joining black  widow is rick mason  in the comics mason is a freelance  mercenary and ex-shield agent  the mcu portrays him somewhat  canonically but one new wrinkle here is  that the filmmakers have given him a bit  of a romantic  sexual tension with natasha in the  comics mason's just a regular shady guy  no super suit involved and that's  basically the version we get on the  screen  having said that his ability to wrangle  up anything natasha needs  is pretty super in and of itself one of  the more striking characters in black  widow is alexei schasterkoff  also known as red guardian he's  basically the russian version of captain  america  portrayed by david harbour although  there have been multiple red guardians  throughout marvel comics history  harbour is playing one of the more  complicated men to wear the costume  shostakov's backstory is a mile long but  the highlights include  actually being married to natasha dying  and coming back as a robot and then as a  zombie  and even taking over clint barton's  ronin identity  in the mcu's black widow shows the  coppers natasha  and elena's adoptive father but their  history together is similarly mad by  betrayal distrust  and emotional pain i couldn't be more  proud of you  you smell really bad general thaddeus e  thunderbolt russ is one of the oldest  supporting characters in marvel comics  history  he's been around since the first issue  of the incredible hulk in 1962  william hurt has portrayed ross in  multiple mcu movies  making his first turner's ross in 2008's  the incredible hulk  first seen as a lieutenant general in  the u.s army ross returned in 2016's  captain america  civil war now the secretary of state  like the mcu's rust the character has  hunted the hulk in the comics  but on the page he's undergone some  severe transformations  in his obsession to defeat the hulk at  any cost russ himself hogged out as red  hulk  hoping to match his nemesis pound for  pound things didn't work out of course  and after cutting a swath through much  of the marvel universe  ross settled into an uneasy hero role  albeit one with extreme anger issues  unfortunately he never goes into hulk  mode drawing black widow  but it's still nice to see the  oscar-winning actor in the mcu  for a long time marvel refused to tell  us he was playing the villainous  taskmaster  in black widow but the trailers showed  the character in action  delivering some pretty sweet  action-packed moves the illustrated  version of the taskmaster has a super  complicated backstory  but then doesn't everyone in marvel tony  masters was a shield agent who was  exposed to the nazi version of the super  soldier  serum that turns steve rogers into  captain america  but in master's case it enhanced his  photographic reflexes  giving him the power to instantly learn  mimic and mirror an opponent's fighting  style  that's made him exceptionally difficult  to beat as he's torn his way through the  marvel universe  when it comes to their outfits the comic  book taskmaster looks a lot like the  mcu's villain  the movie character's outfit is faithful  to the spirit of the comics  if not slavish and execution of course  when it comes to who's wearing the mask  the marvel cinematic universe goes in a  completely different direction  instead of it being tony masters  mimicking natasha's moves  this time it's antonia drakov the  daughter of the villain who's running  the red room  and someone who natasha has run into  before  can you can you wipe out  that much red  drakoff's daughter it's a nice little  twist one that's connected to natasha  romanoff's feelings of intense guilt  about her past and it helps take the  character of taskmaster in new and  exciting directions  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

